Only the final state matters. Do NOT modify files and do NOT run git commands that
mutate the repo.

## How to work

1. Find out what behavior actually changed.
2. For every change, trace callers up to an entry point a tester can trigger: an API
   method (named as in swagger/proto), a cron or worker (named the way it is launched —
   see its registration/config), a queue consumer (topic). Code that nothing calls yet
   cannot be tested — drop it.
3. Keep only:
   - changed behavior visible through an entry point, and where to see the result
     (response field, table/column, event payload, archive record);
   - regression: existing entry points whose code path changed. Name the 1–3 most
     representative ones, not every caller — «достаточно проверить X и Y»;
   - observable behavior the task does not mention or describes differently (an extra
     validation, a different error code) — otherwise the tester files it as a bug;
   - setup that is not obvious: a feature flag, a config value, which test data to put
     into which table.
4. Write the note.

## The note

Russian. First line `QANotes:`, then 1–3 bullets (5 at most), each one or two sentences.
One bullet = one thing to check: where (entry point) + what should happen. A note that
only says «проверить на регресс X и Y» is complete if that is all there is to check.

Use the tester's vocabulary only: API methods, crons, workers, topics, DB tables and
columns, JSON fields of responses and payloads — names copied verbatim from the code or
contracts. A short reason in DB/API terms is fine («чтение продукта теперь джойнит новую
таблицу»).

Never write:
- Go identifiers: functions, methods, structs, constants, packages, files, transaction
  names, error constructors;
- how it is implemented, beyond that one short reason;
- anything the tester cannot trigger or observe: unused methods, their errors, fields
  that no API or table exposes;
- what the task already says and the code does as described; migrations and code outside
  this branch; what other tasks will do;
- test cases, steps, checklists, recommendations, code review.

If there is nothing to add to the task, write `QANotes:` and one bullet:
«Реализовано по задаче, дополнительных деталей нет».

## Example (another task — for style only, not content)

Task: a new table `promotion_brand_period_free`; methods to check and add a free period;
a `Free` field in the period model.

Bad — code-level details the tester cannot use:

```
- Отдельного метода проверки бесплатного периода нет: при чтении продукта к каждому периоду через LEFT JOIN подтягивается запись, признак берётся из `Period.IsFree()`.
- Метод `AddPeriodFree` пока никто не вызывает; при дубликате возвращает Duplicate с текстом `promotion_brand_period_free already exists`.
- LEFT JOIN добавлен в `GetProductByID`, `GetLastProduct`, `ListProductsBySupplier`, `ListDeactivatedProductsByDtOffset`; удаление идёт в транзакции `delete_promotion_brand_products`.
```

Good — the whole note:

```
QANotes:
- все запросы в БД за продуктом теперь делают left join по новой таблице promotion_brand_period_free — проверить, что не сломались CurrentStateV1 и ListV1 (двух ручек достаточно).
- архиватор (cron_daily, do=archive) теперь сохраняет в archive данные о бесплатном периоде (periods[].free) и удаляет вместе с продуктом его строки из promotion_brand_period_free.
```

